  "citation": "(1997) 2 Sri LR 173",
  "statement": "Section 21 of Act, No. 39 of 1981 must be interpreted to deem lands vested in the Land Reform Commission.",
  "supporting_quote": "1. Section 21 of Act, No. 39 of 1981 must be interpreted to mean that lands which vested in some other authority in terms of the Land Acquisition must be deemed to have vested in the Land Reform Commission. Since lands acquired before 26.08.72 but after 29.05.71 were not lands vested in the Land Reform Commission, such lands only were vested in the Land Reform Commission provided no compensation had been paid as on 03.06.1981. Statutory declarations could be made more than once. Act, No. 14 of 1986 which amended section 21 has no retrospective effect. It came into operation from 20.08.1986. The plaint in the instant case was filed on 13.02.1984 and judgment was delivered on 27.03.1986 before Act, No. 14 of 1986 came into operation",
