eflected in a consensual act where as abandonment is a unilateral act on the part of the tenant. (iii) The act of the Respondent (tenant - signing such a deed) (as an attesting witness) is tantamount to a representation or holding out by the Respondent, that the Appellant obtains title free from tenancy rights which works an estoppel as against the Respondent (tenant)",SRC030-s147,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:452:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2001-45-1,commonlii-LKCA-2001-45,(2001) 3 Sri LR 56,LKCA,2001,A higher court should not invite a lower court to form a contrary opinion on a case.,"(i) Since the District Court was of the opinion that this case ought not be disposed of on the issues of law only without any evidence being led, it is not for this Court to invite the District Judge to form a contrary opinion. (ii) Under S.147 C. E C a case to be disposed of as a preliminary issue it should be a pure question of law, which goes to the jurisdiction of the case. Judges of original courts should as far as possible go through the entire trial and answer all the issues unless they are certain that a pure question of law without the leading of evidence can dispose of the case."" 57 (iii) In this case the questions of law are intricately tied up with questions of fact. S. 147 is discretionary in that what is relevant is the opinion of Court",SRC030-s147,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:453:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2001-45-2,commonlii-LKCA-2001-45,(2001) 3 Sri LR 56,LKCA,2001,A preliminary issue in a case should be a pure question of law that affects the jurisdiction of the case.,"(i) Since the District Court was of the opinion that this case ought not be disposed of on the issues of law only without any evidence being led, it is not for this Court to invite the District Judge to form a contrary opinion. (ii) Under S.147 C. E C a case to be disposed of as a preliminary issue it should be a pure question of law, which goes to the jurisdiction of the case. Judges of original courts should as far as possible go through the entire trial and answer all the issues unless they are certain that a pure question of law without the leading of evidence can dispose of the case."" 57 (iii) In this case the questions of law are intricately tied up with questions of fact. S. 147 is discretionary in that what is relevant is the opinion of Court",SRC030-s147,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:454:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2001-45-3,commonlii-LKCA-2001-45,(2001) 3 Sri LR 56,LKCA,2001,The court's opinion is a relevant factor in determining the application of S. 147.,"(i) Since the District Court was of the opinion that this case ought not be disposed of on the issues of law only without any evidence being led, it is not for this Court to invite the District Judge to form a contrary opinion. (ii) Under S.147 C. E C a case to be disposed of as a preliminary issue it should be a pure question of law, which goes to the jurisdiction of the case. Judges of original courts should as far as possible go through the entire trial and answer all the issues unless they are certain that a pure question of law without the leading of evidence can dispose of the case."" 57 (iii) In this case the questions of law are intricately tied up with questions of fact. S. 147 is discretionary in that what is relevant is the opinion of Court",SRC030-s147,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1010:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca-417-1998-f-18.1.2019.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca-417-1998-f-18.1.2019.pdf,,COA,2019,"A party cannot be inconsistent in their approach in legal proceedings, they cannot blow hot and cold, affirm and disaffirm the same transaction simultaneously to suit the occasion.","He cannot blow hot and cold, affirm and disaffirm the same transaction simultaneously to suit the occasion.",SRC030-s772,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1274:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_40_2015.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_40_2015.pdf,,SC,2015,"In a rei vindicatio action, the burden of proof is on the defendant to show that he is in lawful possession, once the plaintiff's legal title to the corpus is proved.","Where the legal title to the corpus is proved, the burden of proof is on the Respondent to show that he is in lawful possession [Theivandran v. Ramanathan Chettiar (1986) 2 Sri LR 219 at 222; Wijetunge v. Thangarajah (1999) 1 Sri LR 53 at 55; Candappa Nee Bastian v. Ponnambalampillai (1993) 1 Sri LR 184 at 187; Beebi Johara v. Warusavithana (1998) 3 Sri LR 227 at 228].",SRC030-s772,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1363:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_appeal_89_2010.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_appeal_89_2010.pdf,,SC,2010,A co-owner can eject a trespasser from the co-owned property without joining the other co-owners as parties to the suit.,even a co-owner has every right to eject the trespassers without making other co-owners parties to the suit.,SRC030-s147,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1401:draftly-rule-courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_4_2006.pdf-1,courts-sc-sc_chc_appeal_4_2006.pdf,,SC,2006,A defendant who fails to move the court to try an issue as a preliminary issue at the commencement of the trial is deemed to have waived objections in regard to lack of jurisdiction of the court to hear and determine the defendant's action.,His failure to move Court to try the said issue as a preliminary issue on such a vital matter will amount to a waiver of objections in regard to lack of jurisdiction of Court to hear and determine the defendant’s action.,SRC030-s147,section-not-found,Section 147 of the Civil Procedure Code,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
